 "notes": "Headline result: 95% CL limit on g_agamma from ALP-photon conversion in the Galactic magnetic field of ALPs emitted by SN1987A, using the paper's new Poisson likelihood lambda_P with temporal information (black 'This work (lambda_P)' curve, left panel of the 'Updated limits' figure, sec. 4). Curve recovered from the vector PDF figure sn1987a_alp_conversion_limits.pdf in the arXiv e-print, calibrated against axis tick marks, resampled to 50 log-spaced masses over the plotted range 1e-11 to 1e-8 eV; the limit is flat (~5.2e-12 GeV^-1) below ~2e-10 eV. The paper also derives a 95% CL ALP-decay limit at higher masses (right panel), but the conversion limit (improved by a factor 1.4 via timing information) is the abstract's headline result. No dark-matter density assumption (astrophysical flux limit). Confidence threshold lambda_P = 5.14 (half chi2_1 + half chi2_2 mixture).",
